{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he shall offer it as a guilt-offering.</b> It has already been explained that the matter of the guilt-offering concerns sacrilege, just as the sin-offering concerns liability for excision. And the Sages have already said that tzara'at comes on account of evil speech and arrogance, both of which constitute sacrilege. For evil speech is fundamentally done in secret, as it says: מַעֲמִיק מֵה׳ לַסְתִּיר עֵצָה (Isaiah 29:15), as they said in Berakhot: 'One who transgresses in secret is as though he pushes away the feet of the Shekhinah.' And of one who acts haughtily it is said: גְּבַהּ עֵינַיִם וּרְחַב לֵבָב אֹתוֹ לֹא אוּכָל (Psalms 101:5). The Holy One, blessed be He, said: 'This one steals from My garments; he and I cannot abide in one world.' And Scripture has already recounted concerning Uzziah, saying: וּכְחֶזְקָתוֹ גָּבַהּ לִבּוֹ עַד לְהַשְׁחִית וַיִּמְעַל בַּה׳ אֱלֹהָיו (II Chronicles 26:16), וְהַצָּרַעַת זָרְחָה בְמִצְחוֹ (II Chronicles 26:19)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:19.552858543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}